 ## Current release boundary
 
-Revision 99 completes `MVQUAL-PAR1` on top of the exact MVKERNEL1 telemetry substrate and PARCORE1 scheduler. Independent domain/selector/target-size same-N qualification jobs now share one global deterministic queue, while each job retains the immutable TARGET-DATA2B scorer, MVIDX covered-mass cross-check, hard-obligation authority, and existing telemetry. Campaign execution constrains nested cKDTree/BLAS work to one native lane/job and reconstructs comparisons/progress in the historical domain/size order after arbitrary task completion. Direct API calls without an explicit resource scope retain their historical native-thread environment, avoiding a 1e-16 Wasserstein digest shift caused solely by process-wide BLAS limiting. Automatic campaign scoring is conservatively capped at four outer lanes because these jobs are memory-bandwidth heavy; explicit larger values remain available for qualified high-bandwidth hosts. The active qualification checkpoint remains MACE-MPA-0 medium, and the execution contract remains foundation-model independent and valid for MACE-MH-1 campaigns. `AUDIT-EVAL-PERF1` is next; GPU performance authority remains deferred.
+Revision 100 completes `AUDIT-EVAL-PERF1` without changing model inference or GPU numerical authority. EVAL2 now caches immutable species/composition/focus/block indexing metadata per evaluation view, preallocates force-tail storage, and uses a memory-bounded batched paired bootstrap while preserving the deterministic RNG stream and exact persisted metric/bootstrap records on qualification fixtures. FOUNDATION-AUDIT1 now shares its DATA3 frame index and per-run species membership across domains, reuses force-square work, and batches tail quantiles while continuing to consume the already-authenticated DATA6 prediction sweep with zero additional model-provider calls. Same-host paired evidence shows about 1.92x faster repeated EVAL2 target reduction, 3.38x faster 2,000-replicate paired bootstrap, and a smaller ~1.06x foundation-audit CPU reduction on the available no-inference fixture. The active qualification checkpoint remains MACE-MPA-0 medium, while these CPU reducers remain foundation-model independent and valid for MACE-MH-1 campaigns. `REPLAY-PERF1` is next; GPU performance authority remains deferred.
